---
/* KaTeX's stylesheet, inlined only into posts that actually set maths.

   It is imported with Vite's `?inline` so it stays out of the page's CSS
   bundle: an ordinary `import` would land in the shared article stylesheet
   that every post links, whatever this component renders. Vite still rewrites
   the `url()`s and emits the fonts, so the faces resolve normally.

   The trade: a maths post carries ~8 kB gzip more than it did and can no
   longer share a cached sheet with its neighbours, while a post without maths
   saves the same amount. Worth revisiting if most posts end up setting maths. */
import katexCss from "katex/dist/katex.min.css?inline";
---

<style is:global set:html={katexCss}></style>
